> Hi Martinique,
>
> I think the issue with your sleeplog is that you have an odd number of timestamp columns.
> The basic sleeplog format expects an even number of timestamp columns 2 for each night in the data. To address this add a column W10, even if there is no data for it.
>
> Thanks,
>
> Vincent
