I think I MAY have found the error being:

1. Not saving it in the right format

For others:

Once you open excel > Open .txt file > Select delimiters > Indicate how each text field is separated, in this case, each text field is separated by a , --> therefore this indicates that the text between commas is a cell in excel > Click Finish

Click save as .csv and not .csv utf

I have made the changes above, now waiting for the analyis to finish

As a summary for the errors listed below these are the changes I made:
- Sleep log csv file should be within a folder, but not in the data file folder or the results folder
- The sleep diary should have equivalent number of days + nights
- The values within the sleep diary should be in this format mm:hh:ss
- I opened the sleep diary in Notepad to manually inspect it:

- I made sure that that each time stamp has a semicolon ie hh:mm:ss (some had hh.mm)
- I made sure there were no spaces between each commas

I then opened the .txt file in excel to save as .csv

Follow instructions above to save.csv
(Make sutre it is .csv and not .csv utf)

I will keep you updated, I'm hoping these changes will work

