Hi again,

Could it be that your data is in the AMI motionlogger format?
I coincidentally received a test file from someone a month ago and remember that I promised them to have a quick look as part of a possible project. So, I just draft a possible solution.

To use it:
install GGIR test version with
remotes::install_github("wadpac/GGIR", ref = "issue1191_ami_motionlogger")

Next, I used code below on the test file. The time and date are expected to be separate columns as you have, extEpochData_timeformat reflects the timestamp if those columns would be merged by GGIR (so don't merge the columns just imagine they are merged):

GGIR(datadir = datadir,
     outputdir = outputdir,
     mode = 1:5,
     overwrite = TRUE,
     windowsizes = c(60, 900, 3600),
     threshold.in <http://threshold.in> = 1.5,
     threshold.mod = 3,
     threshold.vig = 6,
     dataFormat = "ami_csv",
     extEpochData_timeformat = "%m/%d/%Y %H:%M:%S",
     HASPT.algo = "NotWorn",
     acc.metric = "ExtAct",
     desiredtz = "America/New_York",
     overwrite = TRUE,
     do.report = c(2, 4, 5),
     visualreport = FALSE)

For me this runs but I see that without access to sleep diary GGIR is not good yet at guessing the main resting period by which the sleep analyses is not informative. However, if that could be fixed then this may work.

Best, Vincent

